and alert, in no acute distress.\n- Cardiovascular: Normal sinus rhythm; S1 S2 regular, no murmur. Edema: 2+ pitting edema of both ankles.\n- Respiratory: Crackles at the right base and mild bibasilar crackles; unlabored, even.\n- Abdomen: Soft, non-tender, non-distended. Bowel sounds: active in all four quadrants.\n- Neurologic: Alert and oriented x4.\n- Skin: Both hips and thighs intact, no bruising or redness; both buttocks intact.\n- Pain 0/10; none.\n- Skin: Both hips and thighs intact, no bruising or redness; both buttocks intact. Braden 21.\n- Fall risk: Moderate; fall precautions in place.\n- Lines: none.\n\n**Education**\n- Oriented to room, call light, plan of care, and fall precautions.\n\n**Plan**"},{"id":"note_hospitalist_history_and_physical_2026_10_20_07_15","type":"hp","title":"Hospitalist History and Physical","author":"S. Patel, MD","datetime":"2026-10-20 07:15","category":"H&P","summary":"Admission H&P for heart failure with mild fluid overload and pneumonia.","body":"**Chief complaint**\n- Cough, leg swelling and shortness of breath with walking\n\n**History of present illness**\n69-year-old male with heart failure and type 2 diabetes who has had a productive cough and low-grade fever for 4 days, then gained 4 pounds over 3 days with swollen ankles and mild shortness of breath on exertion. Chest x-ray shows a small right lower lobe pneumonia. Admitted for an oral diuretic, an intramuscular antibiotic, a low-sodium diet and sliding-scale insulin.\n\n**Past medical history**\n- No significant past medical history.\n\n**Past surgical history**\n- No prior surgeries.\n\n**Home medications**\n- None\n\n**Allergies**\n- No known drug allergies.\n\n**Family history**\n- Mother with hypertension; father with coronary artery disease. No known family history of bowel disease or cancer.\n\n**Social history**\n- Lives with spouse/partner; independent with ADLs and ambulation at baseline; tobacco: never; alcohol: none; other substances: none.\n\n**Review of systems**\n- Positive for cough, low-grade fever, ankle swelling and shortness of breath with exertion. Negative for chest pain at rest, nausea and palpitations.\n\n**Vitals**\n- T 99.8 F, HR 87, BP 141/84, RR 16, SpO2 98% on room air, pain 0/10 | Wt 88 kg, BMI 28.7\n\n**Physical exam**\n- General: Awake and alert, in no acute distress.\n- Cardiovascular: Normal sinus rhythm; S1 S2 regular, no murmur. Edema: 2+ pitting edema of both ankles.\n- Respiratory: Crackles at the right base and mild bibasilar crackles; unlabored, even.\n- Abdomen: Soft, non-tender, non-distended. Bowel sounds: active in all four quadrants.\n- Neurologic: Alert and oriented x4.\n- Skin: Both hips and thighs intact, no bruising or redness; both buttocks intact.\n\n**Data**\n- Labs: \n\n**Assessment and plan**\n69-year-old male with no significant history admitted with heart failure with mild fluid overload and pneumonia.\n\n**Heart failure with mild fluid overload and pneumonia**\n\n**Prophylaxis / code status**\n- DVT prophylaxis per orders; fall precautions.\n- Code status: Full Code."},{"id":"note_ed_provider_note_2026_10_20_06_03","type":"erVisitSummary","title":"ED Provider Note","author":"J. Whitaker, MD","datetime":"2026-10-20 06:03","category":"ED Note","summary":"69-year-old male presenting with cough, leg swelling and shortness of breath with walking; admitted to Hospital Medicine.","body":"**Chief complaint**\n- Cough, leg swelling and shortness of breath with walking\n\n**HPI**\n69-year-old male with heart failure and type 2 diabetes who has had a productive cough and low-grade fever for 4 days, then gained 4 pounds over 3 days with swollen ankles and mild shortness of breath on exertion. Chest x-ray shows a small right lower lobe pneumonia. Admitted for an oral diuretic, an intramuscular antibiotic, a low-sodium diet and sliding-scale insulin.\n\n**Past medical / surgical history**\n- Medical: No significant past medical history.\n- Surgical: No prior surgeries.\n\n**Allergies**\n- No known drug allergies.\n\n**Social history**\n- Lives with spouse/partner; independent with ADLs and ambulation at baseline; tobacco: never; alcohol: none; other substances: none.\n\n**Triage vitals**\n- T 99.9 F, HR 91, BP 134/82, RR 16, SpO2 98% on room air, pain 0/10\n\n**Exam**\n- General: Awake and alert, in no acute distress.\n- Cardiovascular: Normal sinus rhythm; S1 S2 regular, no murmur. Edema: 2+ pitting edema of both ankles.\n- Respiratory: Crackles at the right base and mild bibasilar crackles; unlabored, even.\n- Abdomen: Soft, non-tender, non-distended. Bowel sounds: active in all four quadrants.\n- Neurologic: Alert and oriented x4.\n- Skin: Both hips and thighs intact, no bruising or redness; both buttocks intact.\n\n**ED results**\n- Labs: pending\n\n**ED course**\n- 0445 furosemide (LASIX) 20 mg Oral\n- 0445 insulin lispro (HUMALOG) Per sensitive (very low-dose) sliding scale Subcutaneous\n- 0445 ceftriaxone (ROCEPHIN) 1.5 g Intramuscular\n\n**Assessment / disposition**\n- Heart failure with mild fluid overload and pneumonia. \n- Admit to Hospital Medicine (Dr. S. Patel); condition guarded but stable."}],"timeline":{"marDate":"Tuesday, October 20, 2026","marTimeSlots":["0800","0900","1000","1100","1200","1300","1400","1500"],"simulationStart":"2026-10-20 08:45","simulationEnd":"2026-10-20 16:45"},"simulationTasks":[],"triggers":[],"facultyBuilder":{"builderVersion":2,"inputs":{"name":"Frank Delgado","age":69,"sex":"Male","mrn":"SIM-30416","unit":"Medical-Surgical 2 East","room":"214-1","heightCm":175,"weightKg":88,"primary":"lpn_lasix","hospitalDay":1,"simDate":"2026-10-20","startTime":"08:45","hx":[],"surg":[],"surgText":"","allergies":[],"codeStatus":"Full Code","social":{"tobacco":"Never","alcohol":"None","drugs":"None","living":"Lives with spouse/partner","function":"Independent","other":""},"studentLevel":"First-semester LPN","complexity":"simple","facultyNotes":"","id":"lpn_lasix","desc":"PO furosemide (Lasix) 20 mg, SubQ insulin lispro (